    "summary": "The complete candidate combines PR240 with the PR238 settings-page dependency and adds optional saved-destination Test. Current Admin web requests resolve trusted tenant and actor, then validate Origin, CSRF and exact fields. Audit logs owns one full saved snapshot, credential recovery, the one-shot synthetic event, and post-send revision confirmation. A four-operation lifetime bounds caller work and retains late reads; the sender independently retains native work until cleanup. App supplies the service and owns SQL disposal. System logs remains an internal, distinct typed output. Six registry drawings change relative to PR240; full-main review also retains inherited storage, container, external, contract, deployment, policy and dependency impact. No new paid resource, MFA, capture, queue, automatic retry, polling or destination Test gate for Enable is added. System diagnostics retain PR240 explicit SystemLogSink composition with unchanged output and failure behavior. The settings service now requires DestinationTestSender and no longer selects a concrete transport. App composition and the real process probe supply OtlpAuditSender; read/save tests supply a role double. No runtime authority, saved Test, or admission policy changes.",
